    "manas-2010:p1151:b001:l001": "Visible мистеген has no established verb reading in the checked edition glossary, primary dictionaries, or same-witness searches. Мисте pistachio / мистедей slender does not establish this form. Entire verse excluded from translated line and word totals. Raw preserved; no invented ear shape. Completion-first first pass: Low-confidence approximate rendering for “Кулактары мистеген,”; nearest corpus parallel was “Кулактары шалпылдап,”.",
    "manas-2010:p1151:b001:l002": "Continues the description of Beijing champions after the unresolved ear-description at1. No omitted descriptive word supplied.",
    "manas-2010:p1151:b001:l032": "Thousand black-eyed captives retained; this row does not itself specify their gender.",
    "manas-2010:p1152:b001:l031": "Ике read as нике, marriage, consistent with initial-n loss documented in edition preface15.",
    "manas-2010:p1152:b001:l037": "Visible мээси жок means without brains/understanding; not emended to ээси жок, without an owner. The maxim is awkward beside the praise of a steed; ашкере rendered clearly.",
    "manas-2010:p1153:b001:l001": "Маңдайым эмес, артымда preserves contrast: not before me, but behind/after me. The next verse denies a following child; no second negative added here.",
    "manas-2010:p1153:b001:l018": "Шек marks a suspected pregnancy, not verified certainty; three months retained as approximate.",
    "manas-2010:p1153:b001:l029": "Enemy gathering is the legible action; no unprinted corpses or battlefield deaths inserted.",
    "manas-2010:p1153:b001:l037": "Name Almambet remains in38, preserving source-row alignment of the quotation.",
    "manas-2010:p1154:b001:l015": "Implicit he refers contextually to Manas from14; sacrifice for Almambet is retained without swapping the two rows.",
    "manas-2010:p1154:b001:l036": "Өрөөн retained as valley, with horse-concealment function. The compressed companion-selection context is awkward; no silent emendation to өрөн, son/hero.",
    "manas-2010:p1154:b001:l037": "Амыз read as намыс, honor, following the edition’s documented dropped initial n.",
    "manas-2010:p1155:b001:l006": "The twelve khans’ peoples are the object, with gathering kept separately in7.",
    "manas-2010:p1155:b001:l028": "Visible коо rendered ravine; not changed to жоо, enemy, to smooth the praise.",
    "manas-2010:p1155:b001:l029": "Visible салбаган is negative: brought no distress to the enemy. Apparent conflict with the surrounding heroic praise retained.",
    "manas-2010:p1155:b001:l038": "Black felt hat and its brim retained as the affectionate image for Syrgak; a Karakalpak ethnonym is possible but not imposed.",
    "manas-2010:p1156:b001:l015": "Алтымыш асый preserves sixty horse-years as the epic age expression; no silently recalculated age.",
    "manas-2010:p1156:b003:l002": "Аты уйкаш provisionally names in harmony; no literal rhyme between Almambet and Syrgak asserted.",
    "manas-2010:p1157:b001:l014": "Capitalized Жаңырык and Жар-Кыя retained as geographical names, without modern identification or silently substituting an English Echo place-name.",
    "manas-2010:p1157:b001:l028": "Lion charge image may be appositional to the preceding tiger; the literal animal epithet remains without an invented extra combatant.",
    "manas-2010:p1158:b001:l003": "Астымдагы understood as ahead of me in the pursuit/racing context, not beneath the speaker’s body.",
    "manas-2010:p1158:b001:l023": "Күпсөр leather powder-bag, edition glossary1839:b001:l038 and Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/күп/. Powder placed against the palate is the epic action, not silently changed to medicine.",
    "manas-2010:p1159:b001:l002": "Subject remains he; Sarala is the printed horse even though Syrgak is nearby. No normalization to another mount.",
    "manas-2010:p1159:b001:l021": "Там is wall in the image of supporting the realm.",
    "manas-2010:p1159:b001:l023": "Таш сайынган is the established cap rank-button formula; not stone worship.",
    "manas-2010:p1159:b001:l028": "Даңза is the record-book in which the prophecy is found; no specific historical archive or scripture identified.",
    "manas-2010:p1159:b001:l039": "Буттап means by the pood, a weight unit; not by the foot. No falsely exact modern conversion.",
    "manas-2010:p1160:b001:l011": "Divine creator and His servants retained on this row; creates remains on12.",
    "manas-2010:p1160:b001:l020": "Stretched silk dress retained literally; no independent assertion of pregnancy added to this image.",
    "manas-2010:p1160:b001:l025": "Урдун interpreted as нурдун, of light, with documented initial-n loss; this is the miraculous conception image, not an identified father named Ur.",
    "manas-2010:p1160:b001:l026": "Light formula continues25; no historical biological account asserted.",
    "manas-2010:p1160:b001:l036": "Коргол dung pellets retained as the counting objects; not euphemistically changed to beads.",
    "manas-2010:p1161:b001:l025": "Кара кезек provisionally a clan designation, Kara Kezek, supported by Eshiev’s comparative genealogy assigning Syrgak/Serек to Kara Kezek/Kesek: https://arch.kyrlibnet.kg/uploads/JAGUESHIEV%20A.M.-6.pdf and https://arch.kyrlibnet.kg/uploads/JAGUESHIEV%20A.M.-5.pdf. Other narrators corroborate the designation, not a collation of this exact Karalaev line. Raw kezek spelling retained.",
    "manas-2010:p1161:b001:l033": "Kökchebich is the horse’s name, confirmed by joined capitalized Көкчебич at1163:13 and the following horse description. Literal blue young goat is not the animal being mounted.",
    "manas-2010:p1162:b001:l027": "Калтар retained as a dark-marked fox designation beside its red coat; the two visible descriptions are not harmonized.",
    "manas-2010:p1162:b001:l041": "Visible чай retained as tea in the sentry description; no silent substitution of жай, place.",
    "manas-2010:p1163:b001:l013": "Kökchebich is a named mount; no goat substituted based on its literal name.",
    "manas-2010:p1163:b001:l019": "Катыра түлүк taken as punishing/strenuous intensity of the journey. Exact two-word form occurs with the next verse in the national-language dictionary; fine lexical force remains qualified.",
    "manas-2010:p1163:b001:l020": "Шейшеби is urine, not bedsheet: Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/шейшеп/ and exact journey/urine-retention horse formula in national-language dictionary printed186, https://mamtil.gov.kg/storage/post/file/93f73d2b0d1e97340369eee4d6fa6cdca210e229.pdf. No modern veterinary diagnosis added.",
    "manas-2010:p1164:b001:l009": "Fox burrow retained distinctly from the marmot-burrow wording on1163; not harmonized.",
    "manas-2010:p1164:b001:l024": "Караган шак элине provisionally overlooking their flourishing people: караган look toward, шак cheerful/flourishing, эл people. Compressed locative phrase remains uncertain; no invented place-name or silent textual repair.",
    "manas-2010:p1165:b001:l019": "Three horses’ tracks retained; the later Kartkurong packhorse accounts for a third mount besides the two riders.",
    "manas-2010:p1165:b001:l033": "Grazed foreleg retained as stated; the subsequent three-legged motion does not justify inserting an amputation.",
    "manas-2010:p1165:b001:l042": "Kartkurong is the named third horse; implicit holder is contextually Syrgak. No substitution of Sarala.",
    "manas-2010:p1166:b001:l029": "Twisting fur remains the literal disguise/action wording; exact construction is qualified.",
    "manas-2010:p1167:b001:l002": "Narkesken retained as the named blade designation, without an invented modern sword type.",
    "manas-2010:p1167:b001:l013": "Калча fearsome/fierce, edition glossary1838:b001:l030–031; not a guessed foreign ethnicity here.",
    "manas-2010:p1167:b001:l017": "Khurasan is the saint invoked in this blessing; no unprinted modern location assigned.",
    "manas-2010:p1167:b001:l019": "Ай туяк is the votive white-hoofed animal designation; not literal crescent-shaped anatomy.",
    "manas-2010:p1167:b001:l029": "Gold eye/ring decoration retained; its precise armor construction is uncertain and not asserted as modern chain-mail specification.",
    "manas-2010:p1167:b001:l030": "Coral stone is a headgear rank-button ornament, with the printed flask-size comparison retained.",
    "manas-2010:p1168:b001:l005": "Аяш is the relation between the wife and her husband’s close friend; rendered accordingly, not literal aunt.",
    "manas-2010:p1168:b001:l009": "Grass comparison for the Chinese retained as the mass/abundance image; no fixed troop count supplied.",
    "manas-2010:p1168:b001:l014": "CONJECTURE: visible Нашап is read as Жасап, fashioned, supported by the exact same-page phrase Жасап салган эмеспи at19 and Kanykey sewing the horse-cover disguise. Raw source unchanged. No independent manuscript collation; нашап as hashish is unsupported and not used.",
    "manas-2010:p1168:b001:l019": "This exact fashioned-it phrase is the internal parallel supporting the explicitly conjectural reading at14.",
    "manas-2010:p1169:b001:l017": "Туура rendered truly in the reassurance to the disguised rider; no moral uprightness claim invented.",
    "manas-2010:p1169:b001:l018": "Rank cap-buttons preserved; no stone-worship reading.",
    "manas-2010:p1169:b001:l019": "Таза in the cap-button formula is finest, following the established project lexical correction.",
    "manas-2010:p1169:b001:l026": "Fox sentry remains literally alive within the planned impersonation/deception; not rewritten as already killed.",
    "manas-2010:p1169:b001:l034": "Visible Туура сууда бөлүм жок retained literally as no division in the water across the way. Exact maxim and relation to the adjacent death reassurance remain uncertain; бөлүм not silently emended to өлүм.",
    "manas-2010:p1170:b001:l007": "Visible таштап is leaving/abandoning, not таштан, from a rock. Place supplied contextually as the object of leaving.",
    "manas-2010:p1170:b001:l019": "Көйкашка outstanding/excellent, Yudakhin https://el-sozduk.kg/КӨЙ/. Not restricted to fearlessness or an invented physical forehead mark.",
    "manas-2010:p1170:b001:l025": "Ankle-bone hill comparison retained as the epic scale image; no metric conversion.",
    "manas-2010:p1170:b001:l026": "Saddlecloth-size hollow comparison retained separately from the preceding hill.",
    "manas-2010:p1170:b001:l042": "Final arms-to-wrestle phrase continues the description into1171; no action invented to close the page."
  },
